  1. [root prerequisite] Ensure dedicated account/group my-solana-project exists with home /srv/solanaghana/projects/my-solana-project and no login shell; reject an unrelated existing account
  2. Ensure platform-owned directory
     $ [root] 'install' '-d' '-o' 'root' '-g' 'root' '-m' '755' '/srv/solanaghana/projects'
  3. Ensure platform-owned directory
     $ [root] 'install' '-d' '-o' 'root' '-g' 'root' '-m' '755' '/srv/solanaghana/deployments'
  4. Ensure platform-owned directory
     $ [root] 'install' '-d' '-o' 'root' '-g' 'root' '-m' '755' '/srv/solanaghana/configs'
  5. Ensure platform-owned directory
     $ [root] 'install' '-d' '-o' 'root' '-g' 'root' '-m' '755' '/srv/solanaghana/logs'
  6. Ensure platform-owned directory
     $ [root] 'install' '-d' '-o' 'root' '-g' 'root' '-m' '755' '/srv/solanaghana/systemd'
  7. Ensure project-owned directory
     $ [root] 'install' '-d' '-o' 'my-solana-project' '-g' 'my-solana-project' '-m' '750' '/srv/solanaghana/projects/my-solana-project'
  8. Ensure project-owned directory
     $ [root] 'install' '-d' '-o' 'my-solana-project' '-g' 'my-solana-project' '-m' '750' '/srv/solanaghana/deployments/my-solana-project'
  9. Ensure project-owned directory
     $ [root] 'install' '-d' '-o' 'my-solana-project' '-g' 'my-solana-project' '-m' '750' '/srv/solanaghana/logs/my-solana-project'
 10. First deployment: clone backend
     $ [user=my-solana-project] 'git' 'clone' '--depth' '1' '--branch' 'main' '--' 'https://github.com/user/backend' '/srv/solanaghana/projects/my-solana-project/backend'
 11. Build backend (include dependency installation in this command)
     $ [user=my-solana-project] cd '/srv/solanaghana/projects/my-solana-project/backend' && '/bin/sh' '-c' 'npm run build'
 12. First deployment: clone frontend
     $ [user=my-solana-project] 'git' 'clone' '--depth' '1' '--branch' 'main' '--' 'https://github.com/user/frontend' '/srv/solanaghana/projects/my-solana-project/frontend'
 13. Build frontend (include dependency installation in this command)
     $ [user=my-solana-project] cd '/srv/solanaghana/projects/my-solana-project/frontend' && '/bin/sh' '-c' 'npm run build'
 14. [root prerequisite] Render fresh units and Caddy fragment into platform-owned staging; validate units before installation. Do not install stale files.
 15. Install backend unit
     $ [root] 'install' '-o' 'root' '-g' 'root' '-m' '644' '/srv/solanaghana/systemd/my-solana-project-backend.service' '/etc/systemd/system/my-solana-project-backend.service'
 16. Install frontend unit
     $ [root] 'install' '-o' 'root' '-g' 'root' '-m' '644' '/srv/solanaghana/systemd/my-solana-project-frontend.service' '/etc/systemd/system/my-solana-project-frontend.service'
 17. Reload systemd
     $ [root] 'systemctl' 'daemon-reload'
 18. Enable backend
     $ [root] 'systemctl' 'enable' 'my-solana-project-backend.service'
 19. Start or restart backend with the updated code
     $ [root] 'systemctl' 'restart' 'my-solana-project-backend.service'
 20. Enable frontend
     $ [root] 'systemctl' 'enable' 'my-solana-project-frontend.service'
 21. Start or restart frontend with the updated code
     $ [root] 'systemctl' 'restart' 'my-solana-project-frontend.service'
 22. [root prerequisite] Configure Caddy site imports, DNS, and Caddy access to access-log directories; stage and validate the complete candidate Caddy configuration before replacing the active fragment
 23. Install validated Caddy fragment
     $ [root] 'install' '-o' 'root' '-g' 'root' '-m' '644' '/srv/solanaghana/configs/my-solana-project.caddy' '/etc/caddy/sites/my-solana-project.caddy'
 24. Reload Caddy
     $ [root] 'systemctl' 'reload' 'caddy'
 25. Execution is not implemented. Stop on any failure. In-place updates are not atomic and have no rollback or application health check.
